  "notes": "びくびく is an onomatopoeic word describing a state of nervous fear.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- びくびくする: to be nervous/scared\n- びくびくしながら: while being nervous\n- びくびくした{表情|ひょうじょう}: a nervous expression\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- おどおど: nervously, timidly (showing visible nervousness)\n- そわそわ: restless, fidgety (anxious anticipation)\n- はらはら: anxiously (worried about outcome)",
